  "name": "FurcoNZ Hotel",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "FurcoNZ is an annual New Zealand furry convention, and New Zealand's first furcon. It began in December 2002 as a small indoor furmeet hosted at private residences, mainly in Auckland, and from 2007 became a weekend camping event at a camp or lodge with scheduled activities. From 2009 it ran much like larger conventions, with online registration, outdoor programming such as archery, abseiling, kayaking and hiking, indoor board gaming and dances, badges, a conbook and catering. From 2014 to 2020 it was held around Waitangi Weekend, and from 2018 it alternates with Southern Paws on the South Island. In 2024 a hotel-based convention, FurcoNZ Hotel, was added, and the camp event became FurcoNZ Camp. It has no guests of honor or charities.",
